{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1179897-help-on-a-scientology-parody-as-a-nephandic-cult","id":1179897,"title":"Help on a Scientology Parody as a Nephandic Cult.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-27T12:11:47-08:00","id":1179897,"title":"Help on a Scientology Parody as a Nephandic Cult.","content":"I just bought Mage: The Ascension 20th ed and i am reading through it right now. As i do this, I am planning on starting my own campaign of Mage when I am comfortable with the rules, especially the magic system. While thinking up antagonists, a interesting idea popped in my head. The basic idea is a Nephandic Cult that somehow became as large as Scientology. The Cult, which claims to a organization based off Kemeticism that worships a obscure cat deity, is actually ran by a extremely powerful and charismatic Infernalist Nephandi. Can i have some advice detailing this cult. Also, can i have some helping figuring out how this cult hit the big time and how the Nephandi got involved?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 01-27-2018, 03:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T13:46:47-08:00","id":1179925,"title":"","content":"Well first, the charismatic leader of the cult is unlikely to be the Nephandus himself. Filling that role himself just paints a huge target on his back. Rather, the cult leader will be a patsy of some kind. I'm imagining just an Infernal Sorcerer; I recommend picking up PDFs for <i>Sorcerer: Revised</i> and <i>The Book of Madness</i> from Drivethru RPG, when you get the chance. The former explains unAwakened magic users (and &quot;psychics&quot;), the latter about Infernalists (and Nephandi, for that matter; the two groups get separate chapters, though there's some overlap). If the patsy is a Sorcerer, he'll probably have dots in the Path of Fascination, and whatever Paths the character's Nephandi backer and/or demon patron will deign to give him. Plus a few social-focused Investments.<br /> <br /> One idea is giving the patsy dots in the Path of Enchantment, so they can arm the &quot;inner circle&quot; with minor Wonders. They are basically like the Wonders Awakened characters can make, except they invariably have only one Effect they can perform, and get &quot;recharged&quot; through some story-specific action, rather than using Quintessence (which Sorcerers can't really work with directly). Sorcerer: Revised explains that better. Point being, it may lead to the NPCs immediately surrounding this &quot;leader&quot; being armed with minor magical items (the leader will likely keep the most potent items for himself, or for the Nephandus). If the cult is like Scientology, it may use chemicals, so the character having the Path of Alchemy might not be a bad idea either.<br /> <br /> The Path of Divination is also a decent thing for a cult leader to harness, as they set themselves up as a sort of all-knowing oracle or prophet. Their image may need &quot;reskinning&quot; to fit the exact ethos the cult is going for. If the cult has a veneer of being &quot;scientific&quot; (like Scientology does), the &quot;leader&quot; may explain their divination as a result of secret knowledge of probability, or the ability to tap into the collective unconscious of humanity. In reality, the cult leader's &quot;science&quot; may just involve cutting open the belly of an animal (or a human sacrifice) and reading the entrails.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that while I've presented a number of suggestions for Sorcerous power this guy could have, it's best to choose only one or two. The guy &quot;leading&quot; the cult is, ultimately, just a front. An intermediary through which the real Nephandus is acting, and who can be thrown under the bus if necessary. Sometimes, the Nephandus might possess the cult &quot;leader&quot; if he needs to interface with the followers directly. And they Nephandi might make appearances indirectly as an illusion of a &quot;secret ascended master&quot;, if the front leader needs an air of legitimacy. Ultimately, though, the intent behind the cult is to allow the Fallen to escape completely if everything comes crashing down. The best way to do that is to make it so no one thinks there was ever a man behind the man at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T14:05:37-08:00","id":1179930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1179897-help-on-a-scientology-parody-as-a-nephandic-cult?p=1179925#post1179925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well first, the charismatic leader of the cult is unlikely to be the Nephandus himself. Filling that role himself just paints a huge target on his back. Rather, the cult leader will be a patsy of some kind. I'm imagining just an Infernal Sorcerer; I recommend picking up PDFs for <i>Sorcerer: Revised</i> and <i>The Book of Madness</i> from Drivethru RPG, when you get the chance. The former explains unAwakened magic users (and &quot;psychics&quot;), the latter about Infernalists (and Nephandi, for that matter; the two groups get separate chapters, though there's some overlap). If the patsy is a Sorcerer, he'll probably have dots in the Path of Fascination, and whatever Paths the character's Nephandi backer and/or demon patron will deign to give him. Plus a few social-focused Investments.<br /> <br /> One idea is giving the patsy dots in the Path of Enchantment, so they can arm the &quot;inner circle&quot; with minor Wonders. They are basically like the Wonders Awakened characters can make, except they invariably have only one Effect they can perform, and get &quot;recharged&quot; through some story-specific action, rather than using Quintessence (which Sorcerers can't really work with directly). Sorcerer: Revised explains that better. Point being, it may lead to the NPCs immediately surrounding this &quot;leader&quot; being armed with minor magical items (the leader will likely keep the most potent items for himself, or for the Nephandus). If the cult is like Scientology, it may use chemicals, so the character having the Path of Alchemy might not be a bad idea either.<br /> <br /> The Path of Divination is also a decent thing for a cult leader to harness, as they set themselves up as a sort of all-knowing oracle or prophet. Their image may need &quot;reskinning&quot; to fit the exact ethos the cult is going for. If the cult has a veneer of being &quot;scientific&quot; (like Scientology does), the &quot;leader&quot; may explain their divination as a result of secret knowledge of probability, or the ability to tap into the collective unconscious of humanity. In reality, the cult leader's &quot;science&quot; may just involve cutting open the belly of an animal (or a human sacrifice) and reading the entrails.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that while I've presented a number of suggestions for Sorcerous power this guy could have, it's best to choose only one or two. The guy &quot;leading&quot; the cult is, ultimately, just a front. An intermediary through which the real Nephandus is acting, and who can be thrown under the bus if necessary. Sometimes, the Nephandus might possess the cult &quot;leader&quot; if he needs to interface with the followers directly. And they Nephandi might make appearances indirectly as an illusion of a &quot;secret ascended master&quot;, if the front leader needs an air of legitimacy. Ultimately, though, the intent behind the cult is to allow the Fallen to escape completely if everything comes crashing down. The best way to do that is to make it so no one thinks there was ever a man behind the man at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good suggestions so far. I do like the idea of making the patsy a Infernalist Sorcerer in it for the money and the power. Since this the CWoD, i might embrace some of the more disturbing rumors of Scientology like them having a prison for cultists who are trying to defect or are starting to waver. Another thing i might do is give them groups of mooks in black suits who take care of their more &quot;questionable&quot; projects, like whacking anyone who gets to curious. I wonder how hard it will be to mix Kemeticism with the pseudo-scientific claptrap Scientologists spout? Also, i should determine if this cult is as big as Scientology is and if so, how could the PCs combat them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T14:17:04-08:00","id":1179935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1179897-help-on-a-scientology-parody-as-a-nephandic-cult?p=1179930#post1179930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good suggestions so far. I do like the idea of making the patsy a Infernalist Sorcerer in it for the money and the power. Since this the CWoD, i might embrace some of the more disturbing rumors of Scientology like them having a prison for cultists who are trying to defect or are starting to waver. Another thing i might do is give them groups of mooks in black suits who take care of their more &quot;questionable&quot; projects, like whacking anyone who gets to curious. I wonder how hard it will be to mix Kemeticism with the pseudo-scientific claptrap Scientologists spout? Also, i should determine if this cult is as big as Scientology is and if so, how could the PCs combat them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another thing to remember is that Scientology often used another avenue of attack to defend its interests: litigation. The church of Scientology is notorious for lawsuits, and for having their more unsavory practices be coached or dressed up to just pass as legal.<br /> <br /> If your fictional cult is in any way popular - even at a fraction of Scientology's popularity - have the cult lawyer up where possible. If it can entangle PCs in legal battles, it's to their benefit. Having secret hit squads is good in and of itself, but so is making the law work for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T15:33:53-08:00","id":1179954,"title":"","content":"Social pressure is going to be more effective overall than whacking people. Oh, and there's an episode of <i>Millennium</i> called Gehenna which has one of these make money cults as the bad guys.<br /> <br /> How much detail you need on the cult depends on how the players will interact with it. If it's not the big bad, just come up with some major beliefs and a few phrases and let the players imagine what's there.<br /> <br /> A larger cult is going to have to offer a lot more, especially if it is secret, than a small one. The bigger the pyramid, the more the followers need to feel they get something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T15:41:13-08:00","id":1179956,"title":"","content":"Yeah, this cult will have a lot of money, so money will probably be spread around to make their enemies squirm. This group is probably gonna be one of the main antagonists of my Chronicle. It will either be a Traditionalist or Despirates game because the Technocrats could probably curb-stomp them with little difficulty. Also, i wonder what kind of demon would take the form of a cat of all things?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T16:17:11-08:00","id":1179967,"title":"","content":"I'd play up the more negative stereotypes about the cats. Greed, Imperial arrogance etc for your 'cat deity'. Is the cat the actual fallen entity itself or an go between to keep people from guessing what they are actually worshipping? <br /> <br /> If this cult has a lot of money, and your trying for an expy of Scientology, play up the 'secret society of the rich and powerful' i think for the SOURCE of their money. Celebrities, politicians and Celebrities have joined up, and are paying money to the organisation. Then ask yourself...what does the cut do to make these people want to play? Secret Knowledge is a good one, but its not the only one. I mean how does the cult draw in new people, especially ones that can pay? Perhaps they have their hands in the illicit drugs trade and get people to come to one of their services to get their fix of a custom drug they are pushing. Perhaps they are providing more unsavoury things (like doing whatever it is they want to those people locked in those dungeons you mentioned). <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11535-furoan","name":"Furoan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T19:51:50-08:00","id":1180029,"title":"","content":"Good ideas Furoan. I think i might do monetary incentives, Secret Knowledge and fulfilled pleasures to drum up recruits. I wonder how to get Desperates or Traditionalists on the trail of this cult?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T20:53:27-08:00","id":1180046,"title":"","content":"Depends on the characters mostly. You have a college student? Perhaps they heard of this amazing new drug that hit one of the clubs last week, and noticing that all the people are itching to get another hit. (and this time all those party goers find out that the drug is going to cost some hard cash this time around...)<br /> <br /> You have somebody working as a Reporter? The news agency gets hit with a massive lawsuit for reporting about the storied abuses that this cult undergoes.<br /> <br /> Then of course you have your magical contracts, such as noticing that the there's a huge amount of hateful or just plane unpleasant resonance near the big compound on the other side of town.<br /> <br /> I like the drug one because it can seem to start small and they realise that this cult is a big thing rather than just one sorcerer pushing a magically enhanced drug, but the massive lawsuits threatening the local news agency, or the cult funnelling money into local elections could be certainly something that catches your character's eyes.<br /> <br /> Another idea you might want to consider is blackmail. You mentioned illicit pleasures that the cult provides but then suddenly they can't back out because the cult has recorded those sessions and suddenly those politicians etc have to work for the cult or they will be personally ruined...or end up in another of those cells waiting for the next 'new recruit' having THEIR turn in doing whatever they wan't to the 'heretics'.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11535-furoan","name":"Furoan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T06:27:30-08:00","id":1180149,"title":"","content":"Those are good suggestions. Also, i feel tempted to make their Nephandic master spend much of his or her time in a labryinth that kinda looks like a Egyptian Tomb. I wonder why a Nephandus would be obsessed with Ancient Egypt,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T06:52:26-08:00","id":1180153,"title":"","content":"Maybe make it so that vocal detractors and critics of the cult in the media regularly join the cult later (or at least appear to do so on the surface) ; most of the time annonouncing it publicly and renouncing their crticisism of the group.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1179897-help-on-a-scientology-parody-as-a-nephandic-cult?p=1180149#post1180149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those are good suggestions. Also, i feel tempted to make their Nephandic master spend much of his or her time in a labryinth that kinda looks like a Egyptian Tomb. I wonder why a Nephandus would be obsessed with Ancient Egypt,</div> </div> </div> </div>It could be that she or he joined the Nephandi while being in Egypt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 01-28-2018, 10:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T07:39:47-08:00","id":1180161,"title":"","content":"Some Setite could have influenced the Nephandi. Not all Setite vampires are from Egypt, but there are quite a few.<br /> <br /> Another Egyptian Nephandi could be a Hermetic <i>barabbi</i>. The Order of Hermes is big into Thoth and has a lot of history in Ancient Egypt. Maybe the Hermetic <i>barabbi </i>just likes those Egyptian trappings.<br /> <br /> For the big bad group, be sure you have layers of minions so the PCs don't meet the big bad leader (the real one) until they've had a chance to explore the cult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T16:10:22-08:00","id":1180272,"title":"","content":"Yeah, a Hermetic Barabbi would be a interesting antagonist. I am picturing a scene where the PCs are in a gunfight with the cult's security forces in a office full of cubicles. I wonder how i can make this scnario for a Technocratic game without the Technocrats curbstomping them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T15:02:56-08:00","id":1180511,"title":"","content":"First off, the Technocracy is a large organization. There's always red tape in a large organization, because managers aren't supposed to do what's best for just their responsibility area. So, there are constraints on any Technocrat's ability to get things done.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy has also been subverted by the Nephandi in multiple sites and at multiple levels in the hierarchy. A powerful cult with a lot of money that wants the authorities off its back will certainly have a few paid informants, problem solving experts (could be called fixers) and a few people paid off to look the other way. So, even if there was not red tape blocking the Technocracy, there could be members of the Technocracy who serve the Nephandi.<br /> <br /> Finally, consider that even if there was a strong Technocratic desire to stop a problem, information on that problem has to be gathered. Cults which are secretive are going to take measures to control information, so the lack of reliable information on the cult could lead to indecision or the wrong decision on the part of the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy is not all-powerful, because it is a coalition of humans working together.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T02:11:17-08:00","id":1180647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1179897-help-on-a-scientology-parody-as-a-nephandic-cult?p=1180272#post1180272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I wonder how i can make this scnario for a Technocratic game without the Technocrats curbstomping them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do you think that Technocrats specifically could easily destroy a cult like this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T09:14:47-08:00","id":1180749,"title":"","content":"I figured that since the cult is pretty large and kinda popular that the Technocrats would have a easier time infiltrating it and destroying it, since they have a lot of control over the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T13:09:52-08:00","id":1180858,"title":"","content":"Nothing could ever beat what the actual Scientologists do. Play it like Pentex in WtA; just look up all the horrible things corporations have done to the environment in scandalous terms and use those, and add some supernatural elements.<br /> <br /> So for Scientologists, they frequently frame ex-members and whistleblowers as pedophiles. That's a thing they *actually* do, almost as routine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}